WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.465 --> 00:00:02.472
Team Polaris presents HEARTH:

2
00:00:02.472 --> 00:00:05.273
fire-safety intelligence for crewed habitats,

3
00:00:05.273 --> 00:00:10.169
built on 847 real NASA microgravity fire tests.

4
00:00:10.278 --> 00:00:11.564
On Mission overview,

5
00:00:11.564 --> 00:00:13.343
pick a habitat and see its air at a

6
00:00:13.343 --> 00:00:15.661
glance. Every page,

7
00:00:15.661 --> 00:00:16.899
and our crewmate VESTA,

8
00:00:16.899 --> 00:00:18.638
follow it.

9
00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.184
Ask VESTA in plain words.

10
00:00:21.184 --> 00:00:23.384
She checks the NASA data with her tools,

11
00:00:23.384 --> 00:00:24.586
cites every source,

12
00:00:24.586 --> 00:00:27.262
and tags how sure she is.

13
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.274
Her answers light up the matching tests on the

14
00:00:29.274 --> 00:00:31.318
habitat map.

15
00:00:31.174 --> 00:00:33.386
Test explorer filters every run,

16
00:00:33.386 --> 00:00:36.510
and VESTA can open any test for you.

17
00:00:39.458 --> 00:00:40.732
Ask her to compare,

18
00:00:40.732 --> 00:00:42.451
and she lines up ACME,

19
00:00:42.451 --> 00:00:45.778
CFI and SPICE side by side.

20
00:00:47.598 --> 00:00:49.617
Safety and gaps shows prevention,

21
00:00:49.617 --> 00:00:51.709
detection and suppression evidence,

22
00:00:51.709 --> 00:00:54.566
and what NASA has never tested.

23
00:00:55.165 --> 00:00:58.278
My data lab checks your own conditions against NASA's,

24
00:00:58.278 --> 00:01:00.309
right in your browser.

25
00:01:00.708 --> 00:01:03.701
Dataset explains every field and lets you download the

26
00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:05.516
clean data.

27
00:01:05.391 --> 00:01:07.903
The flame simulator replays real tests,

28
00:01:07.903 --> 00:01:10.823
in microgravity and on Earth.

29
00:01:11.287 --> 00:01:13.401
About tells our story.

30
00:01:13.401 --> 00:01:15.312
And if an AI service fails,

31
00:01:15.312 --> 00:01:16.790
VESTA switches engines,

32
00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:20.175
down to an offline mode that never fails.

33
00:01:20.023 --> 00:01:23.703
HEARTH. By Team Polaris.
